---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Opener from '../components/site/Opener.astro';
import Section from '../components/site/Section.astro';
import Ledger from '../components/site/Ledger.astro';
import { LAUNCHED, EFFECTIVE } from '../lib/connect';

// The publisher obligations below are taken from each publisher's terms as published in
// October 2026, and are requirements on Eleven One Research as much as on its users. The
// choices behind the rest are recorded in services/data/docs/legal/decisions.md. A lawyer
// should read it before launch.

const publisherTerms = [
  { name: 'SEC EDGAR', href: 'https://www.sec.gov/about/developer-resources' },
  { name: 'FRED, Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis', href: 'https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/terms_of_use.html' },
  { name: 'Bureau of Labor Statistics', href: 'https://www.bls.gov/developers/termsOfService.htm' },
  { name: 'Census Bureau', href: 'https://www.census.gov/data/developers/about/terms-of-service.html' },
  { name: 'Bureau of Economic Analysis', href: 'https://apps.bea.gov/API/_pdf/bea_api_tos.pdf' },
  { name: 'World Bank', href: 'https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/legal/terms-of-use-for-datasets' },
];

const obligations = [
  { label: 'FRED', body: "By using FRED data through the service you agree to the FRED® API Terms of Use. Some series are owned by third parties, and FRED requires the owner's permission before such a series is used for anything other than personal use; the Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis cannot give that permission. The service marks these series as copyrighted when it returns them and leaves them out of its catalog. Obtaining permission for your use of one is your responsibility." },
  { label: 'Census Bureau', body: 'You may not use Census data, alone or combined with other information, to identify any person, household or business, or publish it in a way that does.' },
  { label: 'World Bank', body: 'World Bank data are licensed under CC BY 4.0. If you publish them, credit the World Bank, as the citation the service returns does, and say if you changed them.' },
  { label: 'All publishers', body: "You may not present a modified figure as the publisher's, or use a publisher's name or logo to suggest that it endorses you, your work or the service." },
];

// Quoted exactly from the publishers' terms; tests/data-page.test.ts holds them equal to the
// notices the service returns.
const notices = [
  { label: 'FRED', body: 'This product uses the FRED® API but is not endorsed or certified by the Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis.' },
  { label: 'Census Bureau', body: 'This product uses the Census Bureau Data API but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.' },
  { label: 'Bureau of Economic Analysis', body: 'This product uses the Bureau of Economic Analysis (BEA) Data API but is not endorsed or certified by BEA.' },
  { label: 'Bureau of Labor Statistics', body: 'BLS.gov cannot vouch for the data or analyses derived from these data after the data have been retrieved from BLS.gov.' },
];
---
<Base
  title="Terms of use · Eleven One Research"
  description="The terms on which Eleven One Data is offered, including the terms of the publishers whose data it returns."
  noindex={!LAUNCHED}
>
  <Opener
    kicker="Eleven One Research"
    title="Terms of use"
    standfirst="The terms on which Eleven One Data is offered, including the terms of the publishers whose data it returns."
  />

  <Section label="The agreement" id="agreement">
    <p>{EFFECTIVE ? `Effective ${EFFECTIVE}.` : 'Draft. These terms take effect when Eleven One Data launches.'}</p>
    <p>These terms govern your use of Eleven One Data, a service of Eleven One Research, part of Eleven Hundred LLC. They cover the service at data.elevenoneresearch.com, its tools however they are reached (through an AI assistant, a coding tool or a direct request), and the keys and sign-in that give access to it. Using the service, or letting an assistant use it for you, means you accept these terms, the publisher terms below, and the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>If you use the service for an organization, you accept these terms for that organization and confirm you have the authority to do so. The service is offered to businesses and professionals in the United States, for business use, to people aged 18 or over.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="The service" id="service">
    <p>Eleven One Data retrieves figures from public sources (currently the SEC, FRED, the Bureau of Labor Statistics, the Census Bureau, the Bureau of Economic Analysis and the World Bank) and returns each with a citation to its source. Eleven One Research may add, change or withdraw sources and tools. A publisher may change, limit or stop its own service at any time, and when it does, the service may be unable to return its data.</p>
    <p>The service is offered as a preview. It is provided as available, without a commitment to any level of availability or response time.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Keys and sign-in" id="keys">
    <p>A key identifies your organization to the service. One key is issued per organization, under the organization's name, and may be shared among the people who work for it. Keep it confidential: anyone who has it can use the service as your organization, and your organization is responsible for use made with it.</p>
    <p>If a key is lost or exposed, write to <a href="mailto:info@elevenoneresearch.com">info@elevenoneresearch.com</a> at once and it will be retired. Retiring a key ends every sign-in made with it. Eleven One Research may retire a key that is being used in breach of these terms.</p>
    <p>Use is subject to rate limits per key, stated in the service's documentation, which may change.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Fees" id="fees">
    <p>Access is free during the preview. If Eleven One Research introduces fees, they will be set out in writing, and agreed, before any charge is made.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Publisher terms" id="publishers">
    <p>The figures the service returns belong to their publishers or are in the public domain. The service gives you access to them; it does not grant rights in them that the publisher has not granted. Your use of each publisher's data is subject to that publisher's terms:</p>
    <ul>
      {publisherTerms.map((t) => <li><a href={t.href}>{t.name}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
    <Ledger rows={obligations} />
  </Section>

  <Section label="Required notices" id="notices">
    <p>Every result carries, under <code>notices</code>, the statements the publishers it used require. Where you show the figures to others, show the notices with them. The publishers require these:</p>
    <Ledger rows={notices} />
    <p>None of the publishers endorses, sponsors or is affiliated with Eleven One Research or the service.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Acceptable use" id="use">
    <p>You may use the service and what it returns in your own research and analysis, and in work you deliver to clients. You may not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>resell or sublicense access to the service, or offer its tools or results to others as a data feed or a competing service;</li>
      <li>share a key outside your organization, or use a key issued to another;</li>
      <li>try to get around rate limits, authentication or any other control, or to reach data or keys that are not yours;</li>
      <li>probe, scan or load-test the service, or interfere with its operation, without written permission;</li>
      <li>use the service in breach of law, of export or sanctions rules, or of a publisher's terms.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section label="What figures are" id="figures">
    <p>The service returns each figure as its publisher published it, with a citation that lets you check it. Publishers revise their data, and a figure may change after it is retrieved; the citation gives the date it was retrieved. Where the service computes a figure, such as a margin, it labels the figure as computed and names the reported figures it came from. The service can still be wrong: a source can be misread, a series misidentified, or a value out of date.</p>
    <p>Check a figure against its cited source before relying on it for a decision. Nothing the service returns is investment, legal, tax, accounting or other professional advice.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Ownership" id="ownership">
    <p>The service's software, catalog, documentation and citation format belong to Eleven One Research. Your questions and the work you build with the service's results belong to you. If you send suggestions about the service, Eleven One Research may use them without obligation to you.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Disclaimers" id="disclaimers">
    <p>The service is provided "as is" and "as available". To the extent the law allows, Eleven One Research disclaims all warranties, express or implied, including warranties of accuracy, completeness, merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement, and does not warrant that the service will be uninterrupted or free of errors.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Limitation of liability" id="liability">
    <p>To the extent the law allows, Eleven One Research is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, data or goodwill, arising from the service or these terms. Its total liability for all claims arising from the service or these terms is limited to the fees you paid for the service in the twelve months before the claim. These limits apply whatever the legal theory, and even if Eleven One Research was told the damage was possible.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Indemnity" id="indemnity">
    <p>You will defend and indemnify Eleven One Research against claims by third parties, including the publishers, arising from your use of the service in breach of these terms or of a publisher's terms, including claims about your use of third-party data you did not have permission to use.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Ending the agreement" id="ending">
    <p>You may stop using the service at any time and ask for your key to be retired. Eleven One Research may suspend or end your access if you breach these terms or if a publisher requires it, and may stop offering the service; except where a breach or a publisher requires otherwise, it will give at least thirty days' notice by email. The sections on publisher terms, required notices, figures, ownership, disclaimers, liability, indemnity and general terms continue after the agreement ends.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="General" id="general">
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the state in which Eleven Hundred LLC is organized, and disputes will be heard in the state or federal courts of that state. If a provision is unenforceable, the rest continues. Not enforcing a provision is not a waiver of it. These terms, with the privacy policy, are the whole agreement about the service, unless your organization has a separate signed agreement with Eleven One Research, which then prevails.</p>
    <p>Eleven One Research may change these terms. For a change that reduces your rights, key holders are told by email at least thirty days before it takes effect, and continuing to use the service after that is acceptance.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Contact" id="contact">
    <p>Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@elevenoneresearch.com">info@elevenoneresearch.com</a>.</p>
  </Section>
</Base>
